  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved solid waste management in Zahleh facility.
Number of uncontrolled dumps decreased.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">0 treated leachate of existing landfill.
Limited capacity and landfill, and expansion of uncontrolled dumps in the area.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Zahle Facility upgraded and rehabilitated through the improvement of the leachate management system improved;
One or more open dumps closed and /or rehabilitated;
- The Ministry of Environment and the Municipality of Zahle capacitated and supported in integrated solid waste management approach.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Assessment study of leachate infrastructure, and quantity and quality of leachate generated completed;
- Terms of Reference prepared for the upgrade of leachate infrastructure, and the bid has been launched;
- Technical study, and design for sludge treatment has been launched and its works will be completed by March 2022. 
- The Dumpsite of Hazzerta was rehabilitated and converted into a park consisting of Poplar Trees;
- Project team established, and is coordinating closely with MoE and Zahle, to support in Solid Waste issues;
- And assessment study was conducted to the solid waste facility and submitted to the Municipality of Zahle, highlighting, the performance of the facility, and potential areas of improvement.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Complete Sludge assessment
- Commence with construction works related to Leachate treatment
- Conduct Environmental Studies
- Training and Capacity Building
- The Ministry of Environment and the Municipality of Zahle capacitated and supported in integrated solid waste management approach.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Completed Sludge assessment
- Commenced with construction works related to Leachate treatment
- Completed needed environmental studies
- Prepared materials for training and capacity building
- The Ministry of Environment and the Municipality of Zahle capacitated and supported in integrated solid waste management approach.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">-Establishment of project team;
- Initiation of procurement for leachate study</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">-Project team is established;
-Launched the RfP for the Provision of Services for a Leachate Management Assessment Study for Zahle&#x2019;s Solid Waste Facility</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
